  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-11-16, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " architecture sketch, 2026-09-23, vacant-display nuance 2026-10-17. Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-11"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ". Docs only."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Purpose"
   },
   "children": [
    "Purpose"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "PCDP is the contract for how any spine unit is presented to a viewer, from the smallest honest picture to the fullest one the other three concepts allow."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A viewer should be able to answer three questions from any presentation:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Which unit is this, in which jurisdiction, at which geometry grain?"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Which statements are stamped claims, and of what grade?"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Which parts of the ladder are refused, and why?"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "If a presentation cannot answer those, it is below the minimum. If it answers them for every rung, it is at the maximum. Steps between are allowed. Skipping a refusal to look more complete is not."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Non-goals"
   },
   "children": [
    "Non-goals"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Leaflet, basemaps, symbol design, panel layout, or any other chrome. Surfaces here are protocol roles, not screens."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Fetching data or filling the two examples from live portals. Both walkthroughs are synthetic."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Editing the Master Control Spreadsheet."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Publishing a site, a share card, or an export file."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Making the dossier the name of the architecture. The dossier is one surface that can carry a presentation."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "UK parcels, UK ports, or a claim that the UK atlas’s ",
      {
       "children": [
        "property.html"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " is this protocol."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "How-it-relates-to-the-other-three"
   },
   "children": [
    "How it relates to the other three"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Parcel Identity Spine."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " Defines the unit. PCDP will not present a polygon that has no spine key, and it will not present a key as a parcel when the grain is a footprint or an address."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Context Band Ladder."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " Defines the order ",
      {
       "children": [
        "identity"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " → ",
      {
       "children": [
        "land_use"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " → ",
      {
       "children": [
        "constraints"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " → ",
      {
       "children": [
        "activity_registers"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " → ",
      {
       "children": [
        "derived_readings"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " → ",
      {
       "children": [
        "share_export"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". PCDP does not reorder rungs and does not add a seventh."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Claim & Refusal Contract."
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " Defines grades, stamps, and the three refusal reasons. PCDP displays them. It does not soften them into “unknown” with no reason, and it does not turn a refusal into vacancy."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Minimum-presentation"
   },
   "children": [
    "Minimum presentation"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The minimum is what a viewer gets as soon as a spine record exists, even when every later rung is refused."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "In plain language, the minimum is:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "the outline or the point that is this unit"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "the Industrial Atlas spine key"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "the grain of that geometry"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "one jurisdiction sentence a person can check against geography v1"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "a list of what is not spoken for, naming each refused rung or native key and one reason: not in coverage, not licensed, or not joined"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The minimum includes no score, no owner, no HeavyMap-asserted “vacant” or “available,” and no implication that a refused rung was inspected and found empty. A footprint is drawn as a footprint. A parcel is drawn as a parcel. A source’s own class may still appear later on a filled rung if it is quoted and attributed (see the Claim & Refusal Contract). UI naming for those surfaced classes will be refined later. Display pattern, not final copy: MPAC tax or property class (public in Ontario, HARD-RULES 4) may be shown as a cross-confirmation signal such as ",
    {
     "children": [
      "Tax class confirmed: industrial"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The minimum is allowed to be almost entirely refusals. That is still a valid presentation. It tells the truth that the key exists and that the rest of the ladder has not been earned."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Maximum-presentation"
   },
   "children": [
    "Maximum presentation"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The maximum is the minimum plus every ladder rung, in order, each either filled or refused under the Claim & Refusal Contract."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "In plain language, the maximum is:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "everything in the minimum"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "land and use classifications that are actually joined, each named as zoning, designation, or property class"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "constraints a source states, each attributed to its authority, unsummed"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "activity-register rows joined to this key, dated, without an invented operating status"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "derived readings whose inputs exist, labelled as readings, with method and original units"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "a share/export packet that contains the same claims and the same refusals as the screen"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The maximum is not “every dataset in the MCS.” It is every rung prepared data can fill for this key, and an explicit refusal for each rung it cannot fill. Two neighbouring parcels can both be at maximum and look different, because their publishers differ. That difference stays visible."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Anything short of the maximum is a partial presentation: some rungs filled, the others still listed with reasons. Partial is the normal case. It is not a defective minimum, and it is not a permission to hide the unfilled rungs."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Surfaces"
   },
   "children": [
    "Surfaces"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "MCS Part 2 column ",
    {
     "children": [
      "ui_surfaces"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " names which protocol surfaces may show a dataset. Tokens, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "|"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "-separated:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "selection"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Role: The minimum: outline or point, key, jurisdiction, refusals. The thing a map selection must be able to say before any dossier opens."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "dossier"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Role: The banded reading of one unit, from the current partial presentation up to the maximum. One surface among others."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "share"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Role: A human-readable packet of the same claims and refusals."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "export"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Role: A machine-readable packet of the same claims and refusals."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The word dossier does not appear in ",
    {
     "children": [
      "dossier_bands"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " as a band token. It appears here, as a surface. A dataset that may feed zoning onto the dossier and into export carries ",
    {
     "children": [
      "ui_surfaces"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " of ",
    {
     "children": [
      "dossier|export"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "dossier_bands"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " of ",
    {
     "children": [
      "land_use"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". A dataset that is only a selection outline carries ",
    {
     "children": [
      "selection"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "identity"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Share and export are the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "share_export"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " rung made concrete. They are not a cleaner subset. If the dossier shows ",
    {
     "children": [
      "constraints: not_joined"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", the export contains that refusal too."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Chrome that might one day host these surfaces is unspecified. A future map can implement ",
    {
     "children": [
      "selection"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "dossier"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " without this document naming a library."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "What-every-presentation-carries"
   },
   "children": [
    "What every presentation carries"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Regardless of surface:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "spine key and grain"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "jurisdiction sentence"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "for each visible claim: grade, value, stamp"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "for each refusal: the object refused and exactly one of ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_in_coverage"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_licensed"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_joined"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "no silent gaps and no zero standing in for a missing quantity"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "retrieved_on"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "children": [
      "observation_on"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " both show when both exist. A 2017 by-law fetched later is a current legal text with an old origin. A 2022 inventory fetched later is an observation aging in place. The presentation does not collapse those into “updated.”"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
